#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124287 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "5791bd77-96c7-571d-b8b5-76cb62eb0a9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4228" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{x^2+2y^2-2}{x^2}$ are given by $f(x,y) = c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $c=1$ gives a circle\n\nII. $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n\nIII. $c=2$ gives a hyperbola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y) = c$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2}{{x}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-2 & =c{x}^{2} \\\\ (1-c){x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c = 1,$ then the level curve is $y^2 = 1,$ which consists of two lines.\n\n- If $c = 0,$ then the level curve is $x^2+2y^2=2,$ which is an ellipse.\n\n- If $c = 2,$ then the level curve is $2y^2-x^2=2$ which is a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124288 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/id #uuid "618e7097-38d3-5167-a9d2-5d5a3fc85e0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4229" :question/problem "Sketch the level curves of the surface $z=e^{x^2-y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)=e^{x^2-y^2}$ take the form\n\n$$\ne^{x^2-y^2} = c.\n$$\n\nNote that we must have the constraint $c\\gt 0$ since $e^x \\gt 0$ for all $x.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}=c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can split this into three cases, depending on the sign of $\\ln c.$\n\n- Case 1: $\\ln c \\gt 0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $x^2-y^2 = \\ln c.$\n\n- Case 2: $\\ln c = 0.$ In this case, we have the lines $y=\\pm x.$\n\n- Case 3: $\\ln c < 0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y^2 - x^2 = -\\ln c.$\n\nTherefore, the level curves are as follows:\n\n![](images/5f/5f2ec43639cb31e03cc4a00e43969c7f0333c098fc4b366ea1609772faabfda5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124362 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "fe87d9e4-6445-5ee7-9dc7-6ab8fbb165c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-5968" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $G\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)$ for the function $f(x,y) = \\dfrac{12y}{x^2-y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $G$:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n  f\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)&= \\dfrac{12(1)}{\\big(\\sqrt{5}\\big)^2 - 1^2} = 3}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $G\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)$ is the $3$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=3.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{12y}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}} & =3 \\\\ 4y & ={x}^{2}-{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-4y-4 & =-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-({y}^{2}+4y+4) & =-4 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+2)^{2} & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $G\\big(\\sqrt{5}, 1\\big)$ is the hyperbola $x^2 - (y+2)^2 = -4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a54c10a5-9ef4-586a-8955-c8ef90f8bd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378554} {:answer/id #uuid "3e62eedc-e697-557e-a7eb-17e16f14ea94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378555} {:answer/id #uuid "9b7ce305-e6ff-5ce3-8a7a-084edafec71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378556} {:answer/id #uuid "1b55e37c-193c-5283-9221-71aafd335783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378557} {:answer/id #uuid "14db4b6d-e265-54a1-97c8-5f4f9c459c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b7ce305-e6ff-5ce3-8a7a-084edafec71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378556} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f45af6a-ee19-5560-9c17-22c9bcaae7c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "adad43ad-f556-54b5-872d-89fc29158b9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-128445" :question/problem "Determine the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $P(1,0)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0) & =\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+0+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $P(1,0)$ is the $\\frac{1}{2}$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2 & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $P(1,0)$ is the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2067362d-b2dd-5b81-a0c0-254679d504c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470973} {:answer/id #uuid "85d673ae-d427-529a-a86e-84c5f3aca678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2067362d-b2dd-5b81-a0c0-254679d504c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470973} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d2487c1-305d-5d73-b58d-603c12dd9b35" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf13b53-53c5-595b-b162-9c02134b389f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470975} {:answer/id #uuid "3d4fee56-e3c7-5fe0-b2bf-af7d6065e33d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cf13b53-53c5-595b-b162-9c02134b389f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470975} :answer-field/id #uuid "6697dd78-1361-5fb4-a196-6b0e79a6e315" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9766d54-18d4-55a2-a11d-25dda37f5384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470977} {:answer/id #uuid "e67bade9-f7b9-51f8-8efc-a33eb81a712c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9766d54-18d4-55a2-a11d-25dda37f5384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470977} :answer-field/id #uuid "7014990a-205c-5f78-a1f4-b40b21737c3d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac11e3e9-cb1c-5541-98a0-caa6e8b5b278" :question/math-academy-id "q-129059" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+y}{x}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $c=-1$ gives the $x$-axis, excluding the origin\n- **II.** $c=0$ gives the $y$-axis, excluding the origin\n- **III.** $c=1$ gives the line $y=x,$ excluding the origin\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{x} & =c \\\\ x+y & =cx \\\\ y & =(c-1)x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is the line $y=-2x,$ excluding the origin. So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is the line $y=-x,$ excluding the origin. So, II is false.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis (excluding the origin). So, III is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None of the listed\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c15a454d-c0ca-506d-b884-f5178778ed63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448308} {:answer/id #uuid "c32fe568-db32-54b6-8558-ab5cfc063bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c15a454d-c0ca-506d-b884-f5178778ed63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448308} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5ce8677-ff71-54c3-ad56-f3412cdf488f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449194} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa79405f-ffc1-5234-ad9c-42a8996c0c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448310} {:answer/id #uuid "d901ccba-6ca6-5ba5-b447-d349fd2445c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa79405f-ffc1-5234-ad9c-42a8996c0c53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448310} :answer-field/id #uuid "70ebaa1d-8cd6-5098-9a25-c5f76b89deb4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449195} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5095e664-dc44-568b-aa90-8adbb890de3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448312} {:answer/id #uuid "010f4da8-c1ee-5554-b6b8-f8cf5ae4e818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "010f4da8-c1ee-5554-b6b8-f8cf5ae4e818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448313} :answer-field/id #uuid "93e97ed1-eab4-543d-87b4-43be11f05919" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42b1c0f3-5dd1-53b2-92c2-3218b1cbc331" :question/math-academy-id "q-129063" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{y}{x}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=-1$ gives a hyperbola\n- **II.** $c=0$ gives the $y$-axis, excluding the origin\n- **III.** $c=1$ gives the line $y=x,$ excluding the origin" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{x} & =c \\\\ y & =cx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=-1,$ the level curve is the line $y=-x,$ excluding the origin. So, I is false.\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is the line $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis (excluding the origin). So, II is false.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is the line $y=x,$ excluding the origin. So, III is true.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421492 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cac3057-4676-5ed3-95e8-e4e063eba65b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/ae78f21487e5883b278f0b62a92b2b44ffe8e83e9bd942cf6c94ed4c46d18c67.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421486} {:answer/id #uuid "61cd2c81-8156-5dbe-b41f-65c5a923eb06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e405503abc7c773cde77a3631e3e39ed1693e3aac958731a9a8ae52e618b03fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421487} {:answer/id #uuid "928d4148-96cc-555a-8460-275af511b8a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f9f6a496ebabedfb6f73db014080b64a3830214b337bd61c4ac4f4d996a93bd5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421488} {:answer/id #uuid "b23cb473-4c8b-55bf-98c3-c301ef278556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3d/3d7cde978fe7dd74efe8deb0b7b6e507c7ddf549bb45f1eeda81ee82a8b4a002.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421489} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3cc711-dc0b-5b9e-a281-a519fe0fd7e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ff/ff1117065d7475786dd6c45f71f14d78b32cb3273123ced1adf5a67b750dacdd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed3cc711-dc0b-5b9e-a281-a519fe0fd7e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ff/ff1117065d7475786dd6c45f71f14d78b32cb3273123ced1adf5a67b750dacdd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421490} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a04a0ad-4057-596b-b2f3-8b4c7bc755f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca25fed3-89e3-5069-b0f1-d69395195a30" :question/math-academy-id "q-129115" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=2x+y?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 2x+y & =c \\\\ y & =-2x+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $-2.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/ff/ff1117065d7475786dd6c45f71f14d78b32cb3273123ced1adf5a67b750dacdd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3138b86a-c727-542b-a704-b9f484f1e9c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/51/5155660bc0e9957b1a33cc6fbd933ba10618be07911f9384255bc703f7925ba7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387987} {:answer/id #uuid "61b4423f-aaa4-5e66-8f51-4bfffcff5496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/93cd9ed4c9c1507d1ff828abbb697cd72ab8ebdb7d44a1033d6e99a1eed9e633.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387988} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a86254-f752-5816-a65a-30478823f08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0bedc560b7b18c2a6841313d888dde7349b66f2514ce8c222af7ef2fc0bc9546.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387989} {:answer/id #uuid "78f3fc9b-3579-5680-8f2b-716e781df2f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c1/c115999648577bfb60015f0e54dd0c6d6de22076e87026ba94c49e56207144e0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387990} {:answer/id #uuid "6684aa31-9bf2-51dd-b7a2-03fe9aa6f02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d5/d5e28121cd5847f3119a9fb33a57dd2d86e2f12bff3061ef64182b12c1ace178.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78f3fc9b-3579-5680-8f2b-716e781df2f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c1/c115999648577bfb60015f0e54dd0c6d6de22076e87026ba94c49e56207144e0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387990} :answer-field/id #uuid "bace3461-26e7-51b1-ae89-c181bbb9a42d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "384942ae-d22a-5af8-bd31-df40d8002920" :question/math-academy-id "q-129116" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-x) & =c \\\\ y-x & ={e}^{c} \\\\ y & =x+{e}^{c}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $1.$ Also, note that ${e}^{c}>0$ for all $c.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/c1/c115999648577bfb60015f0e54dd0c6d6de22076e87026ba94c49e56207144e0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124888 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eeacf93-e554-58a5-b0b0-b69b6c92cd8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7c/7c4530dc74747fc0bdae0ca4c8608a72dbf03ca413d4479c8a4b9224246ac01f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321510} {:answer/id #uuid "65ab1147-95f7-57c6-a0f6-195188d68f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b4/b4642ea9b585ac066f2ed904b1bee4df7d1ff3449ba2d09afca8364b58f1dcba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321935} {:answer/id #uuid "6ceac803-4898-591d-8209-d1d92026603a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/ae78f21487e5883b278f0b62a92b2b44ffe8e83e9bd942cf6c94ed4c46d18c67.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321994} {:answer/id #uuid "88bcb675-5baf-5bc6-9fec-a149e6d8836e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/22/22ff469fae1e93c0d805e7443c110c8c56b4f005b0ce2f4a641f19a23dfa3135.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322239} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7b2229-4ac4-5665-affc-5be5302d12bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e49f976cd92eac7780062c7013a29e6acb737d4496a1b61955d7c2ceac96084a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2eeacf93-e554-58a5-b0b0-b69b6c92cd8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7c/7c4530dc74747fc0bdae0ca4c8608a72dbf03ca413d4479c8a4b9224246ac01f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321510} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f7dd4d-866d-5387-af83-8c052dcfbb2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f48129ca-8a2b-5a4f-8600-d7fd45c7c512" :question/math-academy-id "q-35520" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of circles centered at the origin. Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/41/413a11a52ed6a4fc76c2848867d664a63fce24dd39088cdd5826b576d8e7b09c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335762 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213f3b39-3e4a-5037-a0ed-fd44ad862948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/24/24b6123a1f641df32cdc19ec77d999dac5584b9693ae92ce9c1e618f67487473.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333288} {:answer/id #uuid "2527f70b-07b5-5068-8d56-c751798b7b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/57/57f87a716b14698d0087bc65e9abdc04776bd4b7addaaf172a4e5f0a5f38ea6a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333333} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2ad579-41ff-5c47-949b-60d933597acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/836e10a411261b1ef2cb8146aed75c40326f278487e5843c57f10f65b9cc3f05.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333983} {:answer/id #uuid "b396fe3c-e288-51b7-8390-642b434f10a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ef/ef3171d89bff6a2a6ef105f81a9fe60959f2d760634039cd8fb0f70cf8c2cc9e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334565} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c9fa4a-b421-5b11-b4d3-07241c8d5153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7c9fa4a-b421-5b11-b4d3-07241c8d5153" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335011} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fbd657b-a196-55b7-85e6-cbcb244ec565" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6cc7e8a4-946a-52ee-b5f1-ac0fda396a47" :question/math-academy-id "q-64909" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only level curves for $c>0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ {e}^{xy} & =c \\\\ xy & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡c \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡c}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can split this into three cases, depending on the sign of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c.$\n\n- Case 1: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c>0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡c}{x}.$\n\n- Case 2: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c=0.$ In this case, we have the lines $x=0$ and $y=0.$\n\n- Case 3: $\\operatorname{ln}⁡c<0.$ In this case, we have the family of hyperbolas $y=-\\frac{|\\operatorname{ln}⁡c|}{x}.$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of hyperbolas centered at the origin. Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/d3/d330ddb12d1df9d31af3d082b04271d02df381739064a6fe2203dabce358a09f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124553 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62dff73b-1857-5192-ae10-fe22577cbfb4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1fe7f12-1aba-53b8-84a6-c65a5b3db079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1+{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379891} {:answer/id #uuid "757f29e0-0793-5816-a02a-c5609b14f555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2+{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379892} {:answer/id #uuid "03d173bd-9735-589b-ae2b-0f0a570f3cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=1+{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379893} {:answer/id #uuid "2e380ecf-c597-530c-bacd-d038a0e62d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1+2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379894} {:answer/id #uuid "3eeebbe3-4754-5082-87d4-a82c718991e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1fe7f12-1aba-53b8-84a6-c65a5b3db079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1+{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379891} :answer-field/id #uuid "5829d29b-d41b-548e-a76a-f71d52e87bf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae2ee110-6028-560b-b154-cea2add1f458" :question/math-academy-id "q-71193" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $T(2,1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x-{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $T$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,1) & =\\frac{1}{2-{1}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $T(2,1)$ is the $1$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{1}{x-{y}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ 1 & =x-{y}^{2} \\\\ x & =1+{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $T(2,1)$ is the parabola $x=1+{y}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d046747a-b317-586d-8d55-5c90d106b70d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471459} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ae2f16-5c4b-5f1c-bc31-c6238c4fb198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d046747a-b317-586d-8d55-5c90d106b70d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471459} :answer-field/id #uuid "e01cb9ca-cfef-5a04-b8e8-faaa3c67d474" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5c8627-87dd-5f0d-836a-c310a9c4ed71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471461} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf51cce-838b-5461-8589-29027a79ad48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c5c8627-87dd-5f0d-836a-c310a9c4ed71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471461} :answer-field/id #uuid "9af77a4f-7777-5db4-b47d-afe23125eeb7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aadc0f6-aa90-5bee-94bc-57244da99e51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471463} {:answer/id #uuid "46907805-5ba1-518e-903b-c1d4d29ff9d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46907805-5ba1-518e-903b-c1d4d29ff9d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471464} :answer-field/id #uuid "af943ca9-e995-586e-81d8-b5176e4f024d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3aaf864-2fae-5bdc-a851-6e2a3303364c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71398" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=0$ gives a circle\n- **II.** $c=1$ gives a hyperbola\n- **III.** $c=2$ gives a parabola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+2y} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+2y & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a circle.\n\n- If $c=1$ then the level curve is $y=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is not a hyperbola.\n\n- If $c=2$ then the level curve is $y=2-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2},$ which is a parabola.\n\nSo, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de1b2908-d140-5d0a-8262-c958d76bfa4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471471} {:answer/id #uuid "f456143a-b430-5e18-95eb-88219103f545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de1b2908-d140-5d0a-8262-c958d76bfa4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471471} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e697f7-446e-5fcc-ae8a-db378503de70" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472241} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55e41eb5-2115-5b1f-9bbb-e67f510d8e1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471473} {:answer/id #uuid "bf770033-4a57-5465-a9ee-d6d68d54b733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf770033-4a57-5465-a9ee-d6d68d54b733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471474} :answer-field/id #uuid "83576e31-5a8a-5315-8054-127553d4c6a1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad5d90de-a61d-5e9f-a889-d499427c60be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471475} {:answer/id #uuid "9f5c3a1e-f107-5159-ae8f-6ce7a0d2da41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5d90de-a61d-5e9f-a889-d499427c60be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471475} :answer-field/id #uuid "5771a531-83c1-5b90-a459-0ec86b28bfd9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c853fbcf-5be0-5101-8f2a-558cbd4a782f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71402" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=9x+3y-4$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n- **II.** $c=-4$ gives a line\n- **III.** $c=5$ gives a hyperbola" :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x+3y-4 & =c \\\\ 3y & =-9x+c+4 \\\\ y & =-3x+\\frac{c+4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=-3x+\\frac{4}{3},$ which is not an ellipse.\n\n- If $c=-4$ then the level curve is $y=-3x,$ which is a line.\n\n- If $c=5$ then the level curve is $y=-3x+3,$ which is not a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124476 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfd8982d-d859-5eb2-9f35-69af39c04822" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Level Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edb9e29c-19c1-512b-b67b-3c63363893cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d5/d573fdc38a90793a5290862e6cfa5943d982f33ee98800199e04e7200067224d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379919} {:answer/id #uuid "2e884e6f-f213-5463-adf6-1016dc564801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/da/da7c5bc006ec489e9283fcf062f07e2dcc01e72793098bda3f36c2b9bc03fd90.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379920} {:answer/id #uuid "646fdab8-0f60-50f2-ae58-70ccadbb47ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c7/c759002d1e72c53e719ed43326ba6564b435ae7e9a80d29f4614e51f354714fc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379921} {:answer/id #uuid "9e4b569d-919d-5cf9-b068-8191ca16e923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6b425704394d6fcd3090b54a3767b031b728cf4dbc44f9ac9446defe1cdb05aa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379922} {:answer/id #uuid "0a6f9f97-28b2-5b81-9f8c-367ea37c7b39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b7/b79c75fb4de77313ff9ae17938eeabc8b55cca395e6516c09abf6742f9b6a23b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e4b569d-919d-5cf9-b068-8191ca16e923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6b425704394d6fcd3090b54a3767b031b728cf4dbc44f9ac9446defe1cdb05aa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379922} :answer-field/id #uuid "92bec405-4b97-5b51-967a-b30418a002b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dd87390-11b1-5a52-bff2-7394eae160c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71410" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{y+2{x}^{2}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $[0,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider only $c$-level curves for $c\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\sqrt{y+2{x}^{2}} & =c \\\\ y+2{x}^{2} & ={c}^{2} \\\\ y & ={c}^{2}-2{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of parabolas with the vertex at $(0,{c}^{2}).$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/6b/6b425704394d6fcd3090b54a3767b031b728cf4dbc44f9ac9446defe1cdb05aa.png)"}]}
